# Interaction With Other Qualities

Energy systems support:

Strength.

Power.

Speed.

Endurance.

Technical Skill.

Recovery.

Decision Making.

No physical quality exists independently from energy availability.

---

# Programming Principles

Training should develop:

Power Output.

Capacity.

Recovery.

Efficiency.

Specificity.

No single system should dominate programming permanently.

---

# Common Mistakes

Examples

Excessive long slow running.

Ignoring aerobic development.

Ignoring explosive work.

Training every session at maximum intensity.

Confusing conditioning with fatigue.

Energy system training should always support combat performance.

