# Success Criteria

The model succeeds when:

Energy production matches combat demands.

Recovery between efforts improves.

Repeated explosive performance increases.

Movement economy improves.

Conditioning transfers directly to competition.

---

# Final Principle

Energy systems do not win fights.

They allow every other physical quality to be expressed repeatedly,

efficiently,

and at the right moment.

The better the energy systems,

the greater the athlete's capacity to perform throughout the entire contest.